# Normalise line endings across platforms.
#
# The repository is developed on Windows and tested on Linux (CI, containers).
# With core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout writes CRLF into the working tree,
# which breaks anything the Linux side executes directly — a shebang line
# becomes "/bin/sh\r" and the kernel rejects it.
#
# Forcing eol=lf in the working tree for text files keeps Windows checkouts
# byte-identical to what CI and Docker see.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must never be normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.pyc binary

# Keep the lock file's exact bytes; it is verified with `uv lock --check`.
uv.lock text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts, if any are ever added, keep their CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
